rse(new, parent)` is true, swap new with parent (new moves up). Because new is worse than parent and should be higher.\nFor sift-down after replacing root with a better element (less worse), we need move it down if any child is worse than it: while `is_worse(child, current)`, swap with worst child. That part was correct.\n\nSo heap_push condition:\n```\nwhile (i > 0 && worse(hd[i], hi[i], hd[parent], hi[parent])) {\n    swap; i=parent;\n}\n```\nBecause if current is worse than parent, move up.\nLet's retest example: initial [A(5),B(3)] root A. Push C(3) at end index2, parent0=A. Is C worse than A? 3>5 false => no swap; array [A,B,C]. Heap valid? Root A worst (d5); children B(d3),C(d3). Need root >= both: is_worse(A,B)=true yes; is_worse(A,C)=true yes. Good.\nPush D(4): size<k? k=3 already full, so replace if new better than root. Root A(5) worse than D(4)? 5>4 true => replace root with D and sift down. Heap [D,B,C]; children B(d3),C(d3). Is parent D worse than children? d4 > d3 yes; valid. Selected {B,C,D}. Correct.\n\nNeed adjust heap_push accordingly.\n\nAlso `worse` function name maybe confusing but okay.\n\nLet's define:\n```\nstatic int is_worse(float da, long ia, float db, long ib) {\n    return (da > db) || (da == db && ia > ib);\n}\n```\n\nHeap push:\n```\nwhile (i > 0) {\n   int parent=(i-1)/2;\n   if (is_worse(hd[i], hi[i], hd[parent], hi[parent])) { swap; i=parent; }\n   else break;\n}\n```\n\nReplace root: after setting new at root, sift down:\n```\nwhile (1) {\n  int left=2*i+1;\n  if (left >= n) break;\n  int right=left+1;\n  int worst=i;\n  if (is_worse(hd[left], hi[left], hd[worst], hi[worst])) worst=left;\n  if (right < n && is_worse(hd[right], hi[right], hd[worst], hi[worst])) worst=right;\n  if (worst==i) break;\n  swap; i=worst;\n}\n```\nThis moves current down if a child is worse than it, swapping with the most-worse child. Good.\n\nMain loop condition to replace root: If new pair is better than current worst root, then `is_worse(root,new)` true